{"schema":"forgedock.run-event/v1","eventId":"6da92556-b8a7-44ac-aeb1-f998d5f2dc01","runId":"b787f5d0-aae1-420e-bc1f-498e208151e5","repository":"RapierCraftStudios/forgedock-pi","sequence":13,"previousEventHash":"sha256:0583224894371bb034267358c02c8be099c2956a49147d96196123c66682c479","type":"phase.completed","actor":{"kind":"extension","sessionId":"01a04375-b023-7afe-b11c-169780a420f5","leaseEpoch":1},"occurredAt":"2026-08-27T13:45:53.007Z","idempotencyKey":"phase:investigate:1:complete","payload":{"phase":"investigate","attempt":1,"evidence":["The claim is invalid against the frozen base because validation exists before interpolation.","A focused regression test remains warranted to preserve the safety guarantee."],"report":"<!-- FORGE:INVESTIGATOR -->\n## Investigation Report\n\n| Field | Value |\n|---|---|\n| Verdict | **Invalid** |\n| Confidence | **High** |\n| Severity | **Medium** |\n| Task Type | Security Regression Validation |\n| Complexity | Trivial |\n\n### What Was Claimed\n\n`setWorkflowLabel` was reported to interpolate an unvalidated `issueNumber` into GitHub API paths, allowing malformed runtime values to affect transport routing.\n\n### What We Found\n\nThe claim does not reproduce at frozen staging SHA `0b7fcd2c596e05d7a98e57a4464d39aae987f71d`. `setWorkflowLabel` rejects values that are not positive safe integers, and the shared `#replaceWorkflowLabel` path independently calls `requireIssueNumber` before constructing either API path. Existing tests cover valid workflow transitions but not malformed runtime inputs.\n\n### Root Cause\n\nThe source review finding targets PR #199 head `a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3`; the frozen integration base already contains the required defense-in-depth validation. The actionable gap is missing focused regression coverage for rejection before transport access.\n\n### Affected Files\n\n| Path | Finding |\n|---|---|\n| `src/adapters/github-projection.ts` | Validation exists at the public entry point and shared mutation path before interpolation. |\n| `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts` | Normal transitions are covered; invalid issue-number behavior is not. |\n\n### Evidence\n\n- `src/adapters/github-projection.ts:479-480` rejects non-safe or non-positive issue numbers.\n- `src/adapters/github-projection.ts:530` calls `requireIssueNumber` before path construction at lines 531 and 539.\n- `test/adapters/github-projection.test.ts` contains no malformed issue-number assertion.\n- The reported head and frozen integration SHA differ.\n\n### History Findings\n\n- The finding originated from security review of PR #199 at `a618dbaf461e6428180733a2a3c02a10c3c4e7b3`.\n- The frozen integration source contains centralized `requireIssueNumber` validation.\n- Available repository evidence does not show the vulnerable PR head as the current implementation.\n\n### Recommendation\n\nPreserve production behavior and add a focused adapter regression test that supplies representative invalid runtime values, expects `TypeError`, and proves the transport is never called.\n\n### Related Issues\n\nNone identified.\n\n### Decomposition Assessment\n\nDecomposition is not required. One focused adapter test is sufficient.\n\n### Acceptance Spec\n\n- [x] **AC-1:** Validate the finding against the frozen integration base.\n- [x] **AC-2:** Confirm no production fix is required because validation already precedes interpolation.\n- [ ] **AC-3:** Add focused malformed-input regression coverage with zero transport calls.\n- [ ] **AC-4:** Re-review the exact committed head with correctness and security reviewers.\n\n<!-- INVESTIGATION:COMPLETE -->"}}
